{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-02T09:41:53.257Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"f80f11f5e7298385ac19a0ee","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-02T09:41:53.257Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-02T09:41:53.256Z","author":"pi-glm","text":"Duplicate #4 and #5 ownership reconciled. Both competing records no longer lead their descriptions with 'GitHub issue <url>' (the source references are preserved in prose), each gained a related dependency to its imported record, and both stay closed. The imported records keep the gh: tags and github_url as sole owners. Measurement — before: failing run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/41297675184 (2026-11-01T10:29Z, 'GitHub issue #5 has multiple existing owners'; #4 had the same competing shape). After: the same gated dry-run the scheduled workflow runs (pm-github 2026.10.29 as pinned by the reusable workflow) passes against this branch's tracker: fetched 6, planned 6, import 0, update 6, skip 0, provenance-indexed 10, and issues #4 and #5 resolve uniquely to their imported records via provenance-tag. The command is linked as a passing test; its pm-test receipt runs in pm's isolated seeded workspace, so the reconciliation numbers here come from the direct dry-run against this checkout. GitHub API budget was checked before measuring (core remaining above the 1500 floor). Guard unchanged; item stays open for orchestrator close after merge."}]}],"before_hash":"adeb8812fe14465eb715e464a762188d3e14ddf2078563e203eb39924d636e9e","after_hash":"539e18d16346eda2a90513479fdde570356e638ec6c3be3ca17e0b5004d820de","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_has